def update_task_status(self, task_id, new_status_value):
    new_status = TaskStatus(new_status_value)
    if new_status == TaskStatus.DONE:
        task = self.storage.get_task(task_id)
        if task:
            task.mark_as_done()
            self.storage.save()
            return True
    else:
        return self.storage.update_task(task_id, status=new_status)

The AI explained that the function is responsible for changing the status of an existing task. It also pointed out that completing a task is handled differently from other status changes because the program calls mark_as_done() and saves the task.

